    "accession": "PXD054939",
    "title": "APEX2-MCM2 proximity labeling with high-resolution quantitative mass spectrometry in ESC",
    "additionalAttributes": [],
    "projectDescription": "Through the APEX2 technique, we identified MCM2-interacting proteins associated with the replication initiation complex. After excluding proteins from the negative controls, we detected a substantial number of interacting proteins in the positive groups of both cell types. This research establishes a basis for further study on the component proteins of the conserved DNA replication initiation complex and the transient regulatory network involving its proximal proteins.",
    "sampleProcessingProtocol": "The cells were lysed using RIPA buffer (Cell Signaling Technology, Cat. #9806) and then boiled for 5 minutes after adding SDS loading buffer. For western blot analysis, the following antibodies were used: MCM2 (Cell Signaling Technology, Cat. #3619), β-Actin (Beyotime, Cat. #AF0003), and V5-Tag (Cell Signaling Technology, Cat. #D3H8Q), all diluted to 1:1000 in 3% BSA. HRP-conjugated goat anti-mouse (Beyotime, Cat. #A0216) or HRP-conjugated goat anti-rabbit (Beyotime, Cat. #A0208) antibodies were used at a dilution of 1:5000, depending on the primary antibody source. The bands were visualized using Tanon App for Biology Software (Version 1.0.0000) after incubation with ECL cocktail (Beyotime, Cat. #P0018FM). For full scan blots, please refer to the supplementary material.",
    "dataProcessingProtocol": "The raw data for protein identification and label-free protein quantification were processed using MaxQuant (version 1.6.10.43) and its integrated Andromeda search engine for feature extraction, peptide identification, and protein inference. Peptides and proteins were identified by searching the mouse reference proteome in the UniProt database (UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot and UniProtKB/TrEMBL, version 2020_12), in addition to manually annotated contaminants. The false discovery rate (FDR) was established at 0.01, and the inter-run matching algorithm was activated. Subsequent to the search, reverse matches, contaminants, and proteins identified by only one site were eradicated. The screening results were exported and subsequently visualized through the use of Python (version 3.8.3), the online gene annotation and analysis tool Metascape (http://metascape.org/gp/index.html#/main/step1), and the complex network visualization platform Cytoscape (version 3.8.2).",
